 "evaluation": "All three responses rightly judge this pair as a genuine conflict with multiple differences across population (psychiatric MDD cases and healthy controls vs. people with multiple sclerosis), exposure/intervention (measured serum vitamin D concentration vs. self-reported baseline supplementation), and study design (cross-sectional/case-control vs. prospective 2.5-year cohort). Response B is strongest because it selects `population` (studying depression specifically in MS patients vs. primary psychiatric MDD) or `intervention` as primary while properly listing the other differences including `outcome_measure` (clinician-diagnosed DSM MDD vs. survey-assessed depression at 2.5 years). Response A is also thorough, picking `design_or_bias` (case-control vs. prospective cohort) as primary, though including `comparator` in `also_differs` for a case-control vs. unexposed-cohort contrast is slightly superfluous. Response C picks `intervention` as primary, which is defensible, but leaves `outcome_measure` out of `also_differs` despite the clear difference in timing (cross-sectional vs. 2.5 years) and diagnostic method.",
 "ranking": [
  "B",
  "A",
  "C"
 ]
